(2619008, 361482, 27482, '<td valign="top">To be honest, I am not really fond of the composition here, if the railing were to start out in the lower right corner and work itself up to the upper left corner, this would have worked much better at leading the eye throught the picture, here it just simply doesn´t, not to my eye at least and I stop at the two bolts in the front part of the picture.</td>', 'To be honest, I am not really fond of the composition here, if the railing were to start out in the lower right corner and work itself up to the upper left corner, this would have worked much better at leading the eye throught the picture, here it just simply doesn´t, not to my eye at least and I stop at the two bolts in the front part of the picture.', '2006-07-13 14:38:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2619010, 361366, 27482, '<td valign="top">This is cool, but it does remind me of a shot I saw once in National Geographic where the photographer used an extreme wide angle lens and captured his feet also in the frame along with more of the canoe and sky and sorry, this doesn´t really compare in terms of visual impact.  Well at least I am comparing your shot to those seen in National Geographic so that has got to count for something.  Not bad at all, got a 6 from me.</td>', 'This is cool, but it does remind me of a shot I saw once in National Geographic where the photographer used an extreme wide angle lens and captured his feet also in the frame along with more of the canoe and sky and sorry, this doesn´t really compare in terms of visual impact.  Well at least I am comparing your shot to those seen in National Geographic so that has got to count for something.  Not bad at all, got a 6 from me.', '2006-07-13 14:40:47.000000', NULL, 1),
