(2643576, 361015, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very well done!  Excellent perspective (goes almost without saying) and I really like how the focus is so deep, and the lines lead you to the people in the distance.  Nice tones, too.</td>', 'Very well done!  Excellent perspective (goes almost without saying) and I really like how the focus is so deep, and the lines lead you to the people in the distance.  Nice tones, too.', '2006-07-20 19:48:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2643676, 359709, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>Crappy score for what I think is a pretty good representation of Perspective (and a rather clever title, I might add.)  Good solid black background and nicely exposed to get detail in the illuminated candles without blowing the flame.  To make it better?  Maybe have a bit more depth from the front to the back candle and experiment a bit with DOF.</td>', 'Trading Post comment Crappy score for what I think is a pretty good representation of Perspective (and a rather clever title, I might add.)  Good solid black background and nicely exposed to get detail in the illuminated candles without blowing the flame.  To make it better?  Maybe have a bit more depth from the front to the back candle and experiment a bit with DOF.', '2006-07-20 19:57:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2643821, 362147, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>I really like this kind of "perspective" shot and appreciate the double meaning with the perspective of time.  The toning serves you well in that respect.  My biggest nit with this is the opening at the other end so far over to the right - my eye wants it a bit closer to the "third" for balance.  Nice textures and depth.  Good to see you back in the challenges, too!</td>', 'Trading Post comment I really like this kind of "perspective" shot and appreciate the double meaning with the perspective of time.  The toning serves you well in that respect.  My biggest nit with this is the opening at the other end so far over to the right - my eye wants it a bit closer to the "third" for balance.  Nice textures and depth.  Good to see you back in the challenges, too!', '2006-07-20 20:13:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2643904, 359984, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>LOL!  What a novel approach to the challenge!  From the scores, it looks like some folks just don''t step outside their boxes too often, do they?  It may be title-dependent, but this is very clever - your shots show great imagination.  Colors are very nice and rich - I like the yellow of the house with the blue of the water and green of the trees.  I''d have given this a 6 or a 7.</td>', 'Trading Post comment LOL!  What a novel approach to the challenge!  From the scores, it looks like some folks just don''t step outside their boxes too often, do they?  It may be title-dependent, but this is very clever - your shots show great imagination.  Colors are very nice and rich - I like the yellow of the house with the blue of the water and green of the trees.  I''d have given this a 6 or a 7.', '2006-07-20 20:23:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2643992, 359811, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>Oh my gosh!  First, congratulations on meeting your prediction by getting a new personal best and a 6.0+ score!  Second, and more importantly, this is a breathtaking photograph!  The perspective is excellent and the composition, with the soft water and the line of clouds, frames the line of boats beautifully.  The colors are soft and not too overpowering, adding to the peaceful, serene feeling this image beautifully imparts.  Very, very well done!</td>', 'Trading Post comment Oh my gosh!  First, congratulations on meeting your prediction by getting a new personal best and a 6.0+ score!  Second, and more importantly, this is a breathtaking photograph!  The perspective is excellent and the composition, with the soft water and the line of clouds, frames the line of boats beautifully.  The colors are soft and not too overpowering, adding to the peaceful, serene feeling this image beautifully imparts.  Very, very well done!', '2006-07-20 20:36:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2644040, 362360, 30982, '<td valign="top">Heh - without even looking at the picture, I have to tell you I love the title.  :-)  I do like the picture, too.  Sky''s a bit bright, but I LOVE the textures and colors of the wall and windows.</td>', 'Heh - without even looking at the picture, I have to tell you I love the title.  :-)  I do like the picture, too.  Sky''s a bit bright, but I LOVE the textures and colors of the wall and windows.', '2006-07-20 20:51:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2644050, 361303, 26081, '<td valign="top">If you were in Jamacia living it up a bit much... this could be how you see you next drink!  It is all in the eye of the beholder.</td>', 'If you were in Jamacia living it up a bit much... this could be how you see you next drink!  It is all in the eye of the beholder.', '2006-07-20 20:52:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2644100, 359572, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>I remember seeing this one in your portfolio before the challenge.  Liked it then, still like it.  Love the red curves - creates a nice flow to the picture.  What I really like is that Sherpet''s pictures influenced you to look at this plant differently - that''s pretty cool!</td>', 'Trading Post comment I remember seeing this one in your portfolio before the challenge.  Liked it then, still like it.  Love the red curves - creates a nice flow to the picture.  What I really like is that Sherpet''s pictures influenced you to look at this plant differently - that''s pretty cool!', '2006-07-20 21:04:46.000000', NULL, 0),
