(2644609, 362081, 42826, '<td valign="top">great little description there!!!  i have to admit that i agree with you 110%, great story to go along with your awesome photo!  my husband about a month ago did the same thing but crashed because of a CD case...you can check out my photo in my portfolio!!!!</td>', 'great little description there!!!  i have to admit that i agree with you 110%, great story to go along with your awesome photo!  my husband about a month ago did the same thing but crashed because of a CD case...you can check out my photo in my portfolio!!!!', '2006-07-20 23:25:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2644725, 362115, 60995, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> How in the world did you get this shot?  The detail on the eye is excellent - I never knew giraffes had such beautiful eyelashes.  Thanks for sharing a perspective most don''t get to see! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Since a couple of people took the time to ask--this shot was taken at a drive-through park in TX where the animals are free roaming.  I was in one of the park''s open air trucks and I snapped the photo as this guy pulled his head away to much the food we''d given him.  I have lots of zoo-type shots, so on this trip I was trying to make my shots more interesing.  Glad a few folks appreciated it! Thanks!<br/> <br/>On a side note, giraffes have very long, thick eyelashes to protect their eyes from acacia tree thorns while they eat the leaves.  Neat, huh?! (degree in wildlife biology )</td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: How in the world did you get this shot?  The detail on the eye is excellent - I never knew giraffes had such beautiful eyelashes.  Thanks for sharing a perspective most don''t get to see!   Since a couple of people took the time to ask--this shot was taken at a drive-through park in TX where the animals are free roaming.  I was in one of the park''s open air trucks and I snapped the photo as this guy pulled his head away to much the food we''d given him.  I have lots of zoo-type shots, so on this trip I was trying to make my shots more interesing.  Glad a few folks appreciated it! Thanks! On a side note, giraffes have very long, thick eyelashes to protect their eyes from acacia tree thorns while they eat the leaves.  Neat, huh?! (degree in wildlife biology )', '2006-07-20 23:56:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2644861, 359558, 29490, '<td valign="top">Hey hey Myra - looks like you can scratch one of the goals off your profile!! <br/> <br/>Beautiful view and excellent clouds, this is a dandy photo.  I entered a similarishtic photo (ie - water/shore/clouds) and received a similar score - seems voters don''t get good perspective photos, huh? ;)</td>', 'Hey hey Myra - looks like you can scratch one of the goals off your profile!!  Beautiful view and excellent clouds, this is a dandy photo.  I entered a similarishtic photo (ie - water/shore/clouds) and received a similar score - seems voters don''t get good perspective photos, huh? ;)', '2006-07-21 00:26:17.000000', NULL, 0),
