INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2666709, 362210, 48570, '<td valign="top">Wonderful scene here. Great capture!<br/>Congrats</td>', 'Wonderful scene here. Great capture!Congrats', '2006-07-27 03:50:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2667290, 362147, 11854, '<td valign="top">Trading post...<br/>   Very nice perspective! This bridge looks sooo long! I love the name carved into the wood. I wonder if that''s the designer or just some kid doing graffiti. The light and shadow seem to play nice together on what looks to have been a very bright day. Great job!</td>', 'Trading post...   Very nice perspective! This bridge looks sooo long! I love the name carved into the wood. I wonder if that''s the designer or just some kid doing graffiti. The light and shadow seem to play nice together on what looks to have been a very bright day. Great job!', '2006-07-27 10:54:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2668546, 359811, 52336, '<td valign="top">Awesome photograph!  I really love the long exposure effect on the water and clouds, my two favourite subjects by far.  Clarity is just so appealing here, as are the specular lights, soft pastel feel to the colour, and the wonderful angle you''ve achieved for this composition over the water.  Well done, a very satisfying image.</td>', 'Awesome photograph!  I really love the long exposure effect on the water and clouds, my two favourite subjects by far.  Clarity is just so appealing here, as are the specular lights, soft pastel feel to the colour, and the wonderful angle you''ve achieved for this composition over the water.  Well done, a very satisfying image.', '2006-07-27 16:49:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672208, 362541, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is my kind of image and woefully underrated.  I like the "perspective" - but it''s the angles, the curves, the lines, the reflections, and the black and whitedness of it that I really like.  Quiet and understated - and well done in my humble opinion.</td>', 'This is my kind of image and woefully underrated.  I like the "perspective" - but it''s the angles, the curves, the lines, the reflections, and the black and whitedness of it that I really like.  Quiet and understated - and well done in my humble opinion.', '2006-07-28 18:38:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672736, 362541, 52336, '<td valign="top">In response to your request for a comment on this photograph:<br/> <br/>While in general a technically good photograph, with pleasing contrasts, nice lighting, and a composition that shows off the leading lines that are the subject here, it''s ultimately a prosaic image, which is perhaps why you didn''t get the score you''d hoped for.  Add to that the title, and the interest, for me anyway, falls a little flat.  That''s not to take away from what is, as I''ve said, a sound image, compositionally and otherwise.  But, for me, there is nothing to engage.  Perhaps it''s a left brain/right brain thing, where some will appreciate the highly structured lines, geometry, etc., and others will be looking for the story behind the image.  As someone has said, a truly great photograph has to be a <i>picture</i> of something, while being a <i>metaphor</i> for something else.  Not everyone can do that with every image, but in photographs where we are asked to consider lines, shapes, buildings, and perspective, perhaps it''s more called for.  I still want to say that, overall, it''s a technically good photo, and many will very much appreciate just that.</td>', 'In response to your request for a comment on this photograph: While in general a technically good photograph, with pleasing contrasts, nice lighting, and a composition that shows off the leading lines that are the subject here, it''s ultimately a prosaic image, which is perhaps why you didn''t get the score you''d hoped for.  Add to that the title, and the interest, for me anyway, falls a little flat.  That''s not to take away from what is, as I''ve said, a sound image, compositionally and otherwise.  But, for me, there is nothing to engage.  Perhaps it''s a left brain/right brain thing, where some will appreciate the highly structured lines, geometry, etc., and others will be looking for the story behind the image.  As someone has said, a truly great photograph has to be a picture of something, while being a metaphor for something else.  Not everyone can do that with every image, but in photographs where we are asked to consider lines, shapes, buildings, and perspective, perhaps it''s more called for.  I still want to say that, overall, it''s a technically good photo, and many will very much appreciate just that.', '2006-07-28 22:25:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2673719, 362373, 49652, '<td valign="top">This is an awesome photo.  The angle and colors you captured are perfect.</td>', 'This is an awesome photo.  The angle and colors you captured are perfect.', '2006-07-29 11:18:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2674635, 361980, 61679, '<td valign="top">Saw that you were looking for comments on this image so I thought I would let you know what I saw when I gave you a seven.  I thought the technical aspects of this shot were excellant, lighting, depth of focus, saturation, etc.  Looking at your score histogram, I see a lot more 3''s, 4''s, and 5''s than I would have expected.  I think this is because the leading line of the cue stick is so short.  This didn''t provide as much perspective as some folks were looking for.  I myself followed the cue stick all the way down past the group of balls.  However, if you had included more of the cue stick and increased the leading line effect, I could have given this a 9 very easily.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-31 07:46:24.</i></td>', 'Saw that you were looking for comments on this image so I thought I would let you know what I saw when I gave you a seven.  I thought the technical aspects of this shot were excellant, lighting, depth of focus, saturation, etc.  Looking at your score histogram, I see a lot more 3''s, 4''s, and 5''s than I would have expected.  I think this is because the leading line of the cue stick is so short.  This didn''t provide as much perspective as some folks were looking for.  I myself followed the cue stick all the way down past the group of balls.  However, if you had included more of the cue stick and increased the leading line effect, I could have given this a 9 very easily.', '2006-07-29 19:17:15.000000', '2006-07-31 08:46:24.000000', 0),
(2674688, 361791, 47852, '<td valign="top">Just ran across this one... considering what they look like as you drive over them, this is amazing! :)  Well captured!</td>', 'Just ran across this one... considering what they look like as you drive over them, this is amazing! :)  Well captured!', '2006-07-29 19:51:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2675442, 362478, 31403, '<td valign="top">25th isn''t high enough for this!  I didn''t see it, but a 9 in my book anyday!  A little diffusion to take the burned out white off the top of the ball would make it a 10.<br/> <br/>Doesn''t matter now.<br/> <br/>What does matter is you shot a VERY creative shot - excellent interpretation of the challenge.  My hats off to you!</td>', '25th isn''t high enough for this!  I didn''t see it, but a 9 in my book anyday!  A little diffusion to take the burned out white off the top of the ball would make it a 10. Doesn''t matter now. What does matter is you shot a VERY creative shot - excellent interpretation of the challenge.  My hats off to you!', '2006-07-30 01:29:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2675625, 362374, 43434, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting picture .. you have used a depth of field which makes the balcony really out of focus which I think is good ... The interesting thing about a perspective shot is that this is YOUR perspecitve of a sweet tooth ... and I got a big one of those and I like this ... it does remind me of salt crystals and tequila .. (ask your mum) ... a good shot once again.<br/> <br/>The picture has used thirds with the lip of the bottle being on the horizontal thirds ...and leading lines with the balcony lines drawing your eye to the sugar...<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', 'This is an interesting picture .. you have used a depth of field which makes the balcony really out of focus which I think is good ... The interesting thing about a perspective shot is that this is YOUR perspecitve of a sweet tooth ... and I got a big one of those and I like this ... it does remind me of salt crystals and tequila .. (ask your mum) ... a good shot once again. The picture has used thirds with the lip of the bottle being on the horizontal thirds ...and leading lines with the balcony lines drawing your eye to the sugar... Kari', '2006-07-30 04:10:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2678659, 362240, 49326, '<td valign="top">Kannski ekki nógu perspective-leg en vá, snilldar mynd. Mjög góð lýsingin hér, nema kannski það væri gott að fá smá meira ljós í augun hans en það er allt í lagi. Myndbyggingin er líka æði.</td>', 'Kannski ekki nógu perspective-leg en vá, snilldar mynd. Mjög góð lýsingin hér, nema kannski það væri gott að fá smá meira ljós í augun hans en það er allt í lagi. Myndbyggingin er líka æði.', '2006-07-31 06:23:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2680286, 362289, 48717, '<td valign="top">WAY underrated.  Great shot!</td>', 'WAY underrated.  Great shot!', '2006-07-31 14:52:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2681662, 361878, 22301, '<td valign="top">Vikas, <br/>Thanks for your comment on my On the Beach entry, I thought I would return the favor.<br/>Then first thing I notice is the the photo is only 600 px instead of 640 and the file size is 113 kb instead of closer to the max allowable of 150 kb. I find tht alot of photos will get marked down for being too small rather then the merit of the actual photograph. here is the <a href="//dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">link</a> to preparing shots for submission using photoshop, which may be helpful.<br/>As far as the photo I think it is good, I think for perspective they were looking for more of a repeating pattern or something to show depth. Perhaps being farther away to show how large the bulding in may have helped out. I think the composition is good and like the thline in the photo I just wish that there was more of them. THanks again.<br/>joe</td>', 'Vikas, Thanks for your comment on my On the Beach entry, I thought I would return the favor.Then first thing I notice is the the photo is only 600 px instead of 640 and the file size is 113 kb instead of closer to the max allowable of 150 kb. I find tht alot of photos will get marked down for being too small rather then the merit of the actual photograph. here is the link to preparing shots for submission using photoshop, which may be helpful.As far as the photo I think it is good, I think for perspective they were looking for more of a repeating pattern or something to show depth. Perhaps being farther away to show how large the bulding in may have helped out. I think the composition is good and like the thline in the photo I just wish that there was more of them. THanks again.joe', '2006-07-31 21:25:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682472, 360211, 22734, '<td valign="top">A very strong and impressive image and then the bird to give it that extra lift! Very nice work.</td>', 'A very strong and impressive image and then the bird to give it that extra lift! Very nice work.', '2006-08-01 01:47:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2683636, 361074, 28532, '<td valign="top">Leads to the musicians and the sunken gardens!!  ;)</td>', 'Leads to the musicians and the sunken gardens!!  ;)', '2006-08-01 13:09:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686311, 361783, 50641, '<td valign="top">Haha, I get it ;-)  Her perspective is not one of awe.  You did get some nice high scores within your histogram so some people must have understood.  But mostly, you are punished for being too subtle and clever ;-) Sigh.  Better luck next time.</td>', 'Haha, I get it ;-)  Her perspective is not one of awe.  You did get some nice high scores within your histogram so some people must have understood.  But mostly, you are punished for being too subtle and clever ;-) Sigh.  Better luck next time.', '2006-08-02 01:50:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2689892, 362358, 55838, '<td valign="top">I like this composition.  Maybe both eyes would have been cool but it is creative and interesting to see only one - something you don''t see everday.  Excellent focus, lighting, and color.  I might have trimmed a couple of inches off the right of the pic.</td>', 'I like this composition.  Maybe both eyes would have been cool but it is creative and interesting to see only one - something you don''t see everday.  Excellent focus, lighting, and color.  I might have trimmed a couple of inches off the right of the pic.', '2006-08-02 21:25:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2693561, 362081, 50695, '<td valign="top">I''m a little surprised you got even one negative comment, since this is a photography site. If you don''t shoot the moment, then that moment is gone forever. I hate the hostility that is directed toward photographers.</td>', 'I''m a little surprised you got even one negative comment, since this is a photography site. If you don''t shoot the moment, then that moment is gone forever. I hate the hostility that is directed toward photographers.', '2006-08-03 21:09:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2696920, 362460, 23394, '<td valign="top">excellent capture.  don''t sweat the comments about the fence--the fence is the reality of the situation.  as is, the fence provides a natural framing, and the timing of the capture couldn''t be better.</td>', 'excellent capture.  don''t sweat the comments about the fence--the fence is the reality of the situation.  as is, the fence provides a natural framing, and the timing of the capture couldn''t be better.', '2006-08-05 06:02:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2698979, 361471, 61871, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by TheStick:</b></div><hr/><i> This is so interesting!  I''m curious on how it was done. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi thank you for asking it''s done by editing with tube images after I shot The 2 bowls of strawberry :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by TheStick: This is so interesting!  I''m curious on how it was done.   Hi thank you for asking it''s done by editing with tube images after I shot The 2 bowls of strawberry :-)', '2006-08-06 09:24:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2699099, 362117, 44741, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by levyj413:</b></div><hr/><i> I see the perspective, anyway.<br/> <br/>Is this by any chance the Duomo in Florence, Italy?  I have a very similar picture from trip in 1994. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Exactly! Good memory!!</td>', 'Originally posted by levyj413: I see the perspective, anyway. Is this by any chance the Duomo in Florence, Italy?  I have a very similar picture from trip in 1994.   Exactly! Good memory!!', '2006-08-06 11:25:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2699102, 362117, 44741, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by angela_packard:</b></div><hr/><i> nope i don''t see it...what am i looking for? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>To be honest, there''s nothing there. It just sounded like a nice title under the theme description.</td>', 'Originally posted by angela_packard: nope i don''t see it...what am i looking for?   To be honest, there''s nothing there. It just sounded like a nice title under the theme description.', '2006-08-06 11:26:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2699109, 362117, 44741, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by wavelength:</b></div><hr/><i> This image creeps me out for some reason. I think the angle makes you feel like you''re going to fall in. Making your photo edgy is good, but I think this goes overboard and causes a negative mental knee-jerk reaction in many viewers. Especially those with a slight fear of heights, like me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>WOW! You are right to be afraid... those steps are very steep.<br/> <br/>The reason I picked this photo is because it makes me feel like I''m looking into a huge cave, and something could be waiting for me just around the corner - ready to pounce and tear me apart. Sorry if I scared you! :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by wavelength: This image creeps me out for some reason. I think the angle makes you feel like you''re going to fall in. Making your photo edgy is good, but I think this goes overboard and causes a negative mental knee-jerk reaction in many viewers. Especially those with a slight fear of heights, like me.   WOW! You are right to be afraid... those steps are very steep. The reason I picked this photo is because it makes me feel like I''m looking into a huge cave, and something could be waiting for me just around the corner - ready to pounce and tear me apart. Sorry if I scared you! :) ', '2006-08-06 11:29:39.000000', NULL, 0),
